    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nJust updated the neovim from AUR nightly, and on every new directory without one, it creates an \"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\"/nvim/nvim-pack-lock.json file on any directory.\n\nI've had the same config for more than a month with no issue. I don't think it's a breaking change on my part since a dir. named explicitly `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` seems incorrect (the previously generated lock file is the proper XDG_CONFIG_HOME still.\n\nLet me know what logs would be best to find the root cause on this :)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen neovim with a config containing packages. I can share mine via a pastedump if needed.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCreates a file on current directory `$(pwd)/\"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\"/nvim/nvim-pack-lock.json`\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-940+gd55252a3ec\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
